WEBVTT

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:16.320
With this power,
which I have received from Mr. Klondike,

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.320
that miserable Kaito Daimon is...

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:20.660
Mr. Herbert...

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.230
Enter.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.070
My apologies.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.620
We've only just received word.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.460
Kaito Daimon and his associates

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.510
are headed here to the castle.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:34.920
What?

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:35.930
Why?

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.360
Why do they know this place?

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.600
Just what are they up to?

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.460
What shall we do?

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.270
Well, fine.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.020
If they're doing us the
favor of coming here,

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.650
we must give them a proper greeting.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.310
This is acceptable?

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.110
Of course it's acceptable.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.650
This is a chance given me by God,

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.820
for me to reclaim my worth.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.660
Kaito Daimon...

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:22.890
Lost

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.020
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:29.940
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.860
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.200
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.910
Found

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:41.160
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:45.620
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.460
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.550
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.880
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.800
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.510
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:00.850
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.060
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.430
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.900
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.610
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.440
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:15.320
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.450
It's now or never

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.530
That is what they say

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.620
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.290
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:25.450
That is what they say

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.620
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.130
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.340
That is what they say

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.760
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:41.010
Regarding That Man, Herbert

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.010
Look, let's not do this.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.490
We still don't know how dangerous a group

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.160
the Orpheus Order is.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:52.520
Going to the hideout Pinochle

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.980
mentioned is the only
way to see Freecell.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.440
I want you to help Freecell too!

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.020
Save him from the Orpheus Order,

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.910
and from Klondike.

00:03:02.350 --> 00:03:03.350
Klondike?

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.870
I have to come through for Pinochle.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.620
No, I want to.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.640
But...

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.290
You don't gotta worry!

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.290
Kaito...

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.960
Once he's made up his mind,
he won't budge an inch.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.480
You know that, right?

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.760
But, sure enough, not
knowing a thing about

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.510
this "Klondike" guy really bugs me.

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:33.740
This is it.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.940
We thank you for your visit.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.900
Mr. Herbert awaits you.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.150
Herbert?

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:41.650
He's waiting for us?

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:43.510
It opened!

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.910
Please, come in.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.500
They're watchin' us from somewhere, huh?

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.500
Fine by me!

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:52.580
Let's go.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.500
Yeah!
Let's go.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:01.840
He's late!

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.800
Just what does Herbert think he's doing,
calling for us like this?

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.320
What's more, I can't forgive
him ridiculing the dead!

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.010
Is that really true?

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.270
Did Pinochle die in an accident?

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.200
What makes you think that?

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.270
Well...

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:21.060
It doesn't even matter.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.230
All he did was talk.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:25.160
He wasn't any use at all!

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.660
You would ridicule the dead too?

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.120
What does this mean?

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.170
Why are they here?

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.210
Please, this way.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.220
I shall be your guide.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.680
But first, all of you
please put these on.

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.010
Six of them?

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.200
There's one too many.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.270
Please put one on Mr. Yoshio as well.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.900
Kaito...

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.410
A thank-you party for us?

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:07.440
Yes, that is what Mr. Herbert seeks.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.650
That is super suspicious.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.500
This is the location.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:26.220
What is this?

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.390
This area is below the castle?

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.810
I, Ana, think this doesn't
seem like a thank-you party.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.180
Well, these things happen.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:41.070
Please enjoy yourselves.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.070
Welcome, all of you.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:50.190
This party is to thank you
for being icing on my cake,

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.080
waltzing in here on
the eve of my victory.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.830
First, I would like to
properly gauge the ability

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.380
of he who has continually thwarted me...

00:05:58.380 --> 00:05:59.710
Kaito Daimon.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.960
Bastard, you're Herbert?

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:07.220
Still, by having you use
your abilities in earnest,

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:11.720
I was instead made aware
of my own inadequacies.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.850
It's rather ironic.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.610
He has two Orpheus Rings!

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:23.980
What?!

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:25.680
What's going on?

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.990
And those of you watching
this on the monitor,

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.200
I give you a chance for reflection.

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:37.250
I am the only one to
whom Mr. Klondike has

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.470
given permission for double Rings.

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:42.340
The difference between my power
and yours will be made clear,

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.120
and just how little you
have known your place

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.460
shall be driven home to you!

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.220
What are you doing, idiot?!

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:52.360
Just one Ring puts incredible
strain on your mind!

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.770
And now, I will have
you challenge a puzzle

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:59.530
made by the truly unique
individual that is me!

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.020
You should be grateful.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.250
Within this castle, puzzles are built
into every nook and cranny.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:10.480
Today, I have personally
rebuilt one of these.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.030
Just for you, yes?

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:14.780
Look, just hurry and
take those Rings off.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.050
It's not like more is better!

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.630
Is this the jealousy of
one who does not own them?

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:21.540
Or have you started to grow afraid?

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:23.040
That ain't it!

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:26.920
Your only way to escape here
is to solve the puzzle.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.420
Why not just accept the challenge?

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.590
Fine, I get it.

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.760
I've gotta escape from here, right?

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.150
That is correct.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.060
I will explain the rules.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.010
The exit is at the opposite shore.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:43.160
You may use that canoe.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.930
However, it only seats two.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:47.190
And now, I shall command you

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:52.030
on precepts that you
absolutely must obey.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.410
Cubik Galois, you will become God.

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:57.530
Huh? God?

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:02.550
Ana Gram, you're a devil.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:03.440
Huh?

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.140
Nonoha Itou, an angel.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.250
Gammon Sakanoue, an archdevil.

00:08:13.370 --> 00:08:16.800
Kaito Daimon, you, bastard,
are an archangel.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.430
Wait a minute!

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.970
I'm the angel, right?

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.240
What's this with Daimoron?!

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:22.890
Shut up!

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:28.230
And as the most pure,
most inept of humans...

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:29.900
Yoshio!

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:34.270
I shall now explain the divine providence
that governs this puzzle.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:35.660
Listen closely.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.420
If the archdevil does not have

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:40.890
the archangel at its side,
the angel is devoured.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:43.530
And if the archangel is not
at the archdevil's side,

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:45.620
the devil is devoured.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.690
If the human does not
receive God's protection,

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:51.420
he is devoured by all angels and devils.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:53.630
A logic puzzle, huh?

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:57.290
Without the archangel, the
archdevil eats the angel.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:00.450
Without the archdevil, the
archangel eats the devil.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:06.520
And without God,
all the angels and devils eat the human?

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.150
That's kind of a weird setting.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:11.900
And the canoe is rigged such that

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:16.910
only the archangel and
archdevil can pilot it.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.490
It can take be used
eight times, round-trip.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.580
If you break the rules,

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.660
this underground cavern
will instantly collapse

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.420
and you fools will all be swallowed up.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:28.080
Understood.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.250
But I have a condition of my own.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:35.170
If I solve this puzzle,
let me talk to Freecell one on one.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.550
Very well.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:44.470
While you're at it, perhaps
you should be told

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:47.110
all the secrets of the Orpheus Order.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.060
If you can make it out alive, that is.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.270
The weight of my hatred for you,

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.650
my resolve to exact revenge...

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.360
Know full well I shall
take your life for this,

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.640
Kaito Daimon.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:04.950
The red eye...

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.120
If I don't finish this fast,
his life could be in danger.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:09.430
You're right.

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.960
Well, at least the
puzzle is on the level.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:13.630
Can't say much for the casting though.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:16.720
S..Say, can't we just cross in order?

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:19.960
First, Gammon takes Ana,

00:10:19.960 --> 00:10:22.530
then Kaito takes me...

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.580
If we do that, when we
reach the opposite shore,

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.680
the archangel will eat the devil.

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:29.690
Kaito will eat Ana?!

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:31.990
You're reacting to the wrong thing!

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:32.690
Oh, my...

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:34.320
Ana, you cut it out too.
Oh, my...

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:37.780
Well, if Kaito takes Yoshio across...

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.280
Kaito and Yoshio?!

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.410
Gammon, you'd eat me?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:45.500
No!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:48.500
The archdevil e..e..eats the angel,

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:49.870
so Nonoha, you eat me,

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.960
I mean, I, you and I...

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:54.150
He is our Giver.

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:56.950
Who knows what kind of
cheap tricks he'll pull?

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.470
We can't let our guard down.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.970
Puzzle time...

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:02.490
Let's begin.

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:11.250
So, first, the archdevil,
me, will take

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.730
Ana the devil to the other side,

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.360
okay?

00:11:14.810 --> 00:11:15.730
Yeah.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.360
Oh, it's moving!

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.990
Make it go faster!

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:24.360
Yeah, that ain't possible.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:25.760
There...

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.940
Bye-bye, see you again!

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.660
Don't eat Nonoha!

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:30.600
I..I won't...

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:31.620
I won't eat her!

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:37.150
I get it.

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:39.660
Right now, no one can get eaten.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.380
Oh, so maybe...

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.020
Is it Kaito and me next?

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:45.240
It is, right?

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:47.450
Yeah, I'm getting the hang of this.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.730
I'm pretty good, huh?

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:50.390
Huh?

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.770
Everything's gone fine so far, but...

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:01.280
That is good.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.860
At this rate, when you reach the end...

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.530
you lose, fools.

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:09.750
Well, sorry for the wait.

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:11.580
You're up next.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.000
Huh? What is it, Kaito?

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:15.800
Kaito?

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:17.540
What is it?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.050
Something doesn't sit right.

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.390
Whist!

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:27.300
What's the meaning of this?

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.270
Why did Mr. Klondike
give him another Ring?

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:33.470
You doubt Mr. Klondike's thinking?

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.240
Uh, no...

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:37.440
Then tell us this:

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.650
Is that the same Ring we have?

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:42.240
No.

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:45.240
So, Herbert was given a Replica?

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:46.740
Yes.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:50.550
Just what is Mr. Klondike thinking?

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:55.950
Is the puzzle not going well?

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.500
No, everything's fine.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:12:58.890
Then-

00:12:58.890 --> 00:13:00.380
It's too fine.

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:04.010
Sure enough, at this rate,
it won't even take eight trips.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:07.010
Maybe they're planning some kinda trick.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:08.880
What are you doing?

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:10.890
Hurry up and make your next move!

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:12.510
Kaito!

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.470
There's a strange hole over here!

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:17.860
Here, too!

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:18.730
What?

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.530
I'll send you a picture now!

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:24.280
That's it?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.410
What is it?

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.010
It's...

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:31.000
Are these related to the puzzle?

00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:34.840
If so, what are the holes for?

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:37.200
They...

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:38.590
That shape...

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:41.320
Got it.

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.410
Nonoha, is anything
different about this area

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.010
from when we first arrived?

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:48.590
Anything different?

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.990
Come to think of it, something...

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.230
That block over there!

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.680
I don't think it was there at first.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:58.730
Okay.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:01.610
This, right?

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:03.980
I knew it.

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.280
Huh? Angel and devil?

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.820
That's right, this is
probably a key to the exit.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:09.910
We're movin' it, Gammon!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:11.490
Yeah!

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:13.250
Congratulations.

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.200
You did well, noticing that key.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.670
Excellent work, Kaito Daimon.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.290
No, this ain't just a key.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.050
Look!

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:27.050
Huh? There's more of them!

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.930
Another angel and devil each.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:33.550
That means, this "key" has been
given the role of one of us!

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.970
So, if we held that thing

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:38.690
and two of us rode the
canoe, it'd all be over?

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:40.980
What's the idea? That's cheating!

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:45.270
Well, fine.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:46.620
It's not over yet.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:48.570
Not yet.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.070
I don't care for this.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:51.380
What a debacle.

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:52.490
That damn Herbert.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.410
I can't watch this anymore.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:57.160
Mr. Freecell, you're staying?

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:00.350
Well, Kaito is still battling.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.920
If he wins, he'll come and see me.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.010
Welcome!

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:12.750
As always, that guy makes some
vicious puzzles, huh?

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:16.140
No, this isn't just the
same old kind of trickery.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:19.640
It's made so that this
can be solved if you

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:21.730
notice it won't take eight trips,

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:26.440
and you assume the number
of "players" will increase.

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:31.060
What's more, if you don't
notice that by the third trip,

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:32.740
there's no way you'll solve it.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.990
This is an interesting puzzle.

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:36.860
Good work!

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:40.580
Once I bring Yoshio over,
we'll be finished, right?

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:41.290
Yeah.

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.080
It's totally dark!

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:48.740
At this rate, my ambition
of ascending to the

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:50.920
top of the next Orpheus Order echelon,

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:55.510
of standing at the peak
of the world will be...

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:13.230
Kaito Daimon,

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:16.470
for interfering with me,
before whom even

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:18.620
God Himself would bow,

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:20.740
I issue this divine punishment:

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.400
The role of archangel attributed to

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.420
Kaito Daimon goes to Cubik Galois.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:31.280
I give it to Cubik Galois,
and instead change

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:33.670
Kaito Daimon's role to False God!

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:34.430
What?

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:39.010
However, as False God, you will later
be given divine punishment.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:42.140
Your appearance may become
that of a loathsome frog.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.060
The time limit is three minutes!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.150
Three minutes?!

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:50.220
This is reckless, Kaito!

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:51.460
No, don't!

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:52.890
You're really goin'?!

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:55.320
Yeah, I ain't gonna lose!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:00.870
There's no way he can make it in
three minutes in that boat.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:02.910
What does he think he's doing?

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:04.790
All we can do is trust him.

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.890
I will solve this.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:13.800
I'll rescue Freecell
from the Orpheus Order.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:15.590
I'll save him!

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:19.430
The key has been delivered
into your hands.

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:24.180
Abandon Kaito Daimon and
you can save yourselves.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.090
Don't insult us!

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:29.690
Kaito is sure to solve your puzzle,
no matter how much you cheat!

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:32.530
"Cheat," you say?

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:36.780
Fools such as yourselves
may think as such,

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:39.610
but having received power
surpassing God Himself,

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.290
I am able to solve it!

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.810
All of you should ponder how to solve it

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:47.710
along with Kaito, in the next world!

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:52.270
That will enrich the way
in which Kaito Daimon,

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:54.580
lamenting in his misery, shall die.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:56.850
Above you all, far and wide...

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:00.840
I will reign supreme!

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:02.260
Is this the answer?

00:18:02.530 --> 00:18:03.220
What?

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.650
You noticed?

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:10.730
I'm countin' on ya, Yoshio!

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.110
Here goes!

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:26.250
Go, Yoshio!

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:27.470
Great job!

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:29.460
All right, we can do it.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:36.720
Damn you, Kaito Daimon!

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.430
Kaito!

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:48.870
Kaito?

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.180
Are you all right?

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.900
Yeah, looks like I made it somehow.

00:18:56.310 --> 00:18:57.400
Thank goodness.

00:18:57.810 --> 00:18:59.790
That's the double Rings at work.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:03.540
We have obtained some all-new,
extremely interesting data.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:06.240
Kaito!

00:19:07.690 --> 00:19:09.450
So, this goes in the keyhole?

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:11.130
Let's try it!

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:17.250
Herbert...

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:24.430
Kaito, what are you doing?

00:19:25.040 --> 00:19:26.240
Back soon.

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:27.930
I've got something left to do.

00:19:29.830 --> 00:19:31.360
You go on ahead!

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.820
Not yet...

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:35.360
It's not over yet.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:41.980
I must at least resolve the hatred
I hold for Kaito Daimon.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.590
I...

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:50.040
That was a good puzzle.

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:53.540
Enough foolishness!

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:56.800
True, I'm kind of a foolish guy.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.880
But when it comes to
puzzles, I'm all business.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:03.390
It was fun, your puzzle.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:05.890
What was that?

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:11.310
You have a lot of puzzles
still locked up inside you.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:15.180
You gotta let 'em free.

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:21.940
You're the man who has come
closest to the Phi-Brain?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.700
I can't approach you at all.

00:20:27.060 --> 00:20:29.190
Should I meet you again,

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:32.210
would you do the honor of battling me?

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.710
Of course.

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:37.800
In that case, I shall make
a puzzle that will vex you,

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:42.710
make you stamp your feet in frustration.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.220
It will be grand.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:47.800
Yeah.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.260
Is that what you thought I'd say?

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:55.980
The hatred I have for you
won't be so easily tempered!

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.520
Hey, wait!

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:59.480
What am I saying, not of my own accord?!

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:00.860
Bastard!

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:03.230
"Good puzzle," my foot!

00:21:03.230 --> 00:21:08.740
For me, a good puzzle is one
that sends you straight to Hell!

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:11.370
No! What's going on?

00:21:12.530 --> 00:21:14.060
That bastard!

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:16.060
Sure enough, it was all a trick, huh?!

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:17.380
Kaito, let's get out of here!

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:20.390
You can't escape.

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:22.760
I'm going to bring down
this underground cavern!

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:24.170
What was that?!

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:25.430
Don't!

00:21:25.910 --> 00:21:28.010
If it means burying you,

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.720
I'll offer myself up over and over again!

00:21:31.340 --> 00:21:32.950
Stop it! Stop!

00:21:32.950 --> 00:21:34.010
What am I doing?!

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:38.260
Kaito!

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:40.040
This is bad! Right now,
we gotta run for it!

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.940
Kaito, go!

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.940
Farewell, Kaito Daimon!

00:22:01.350 --> 00:22:04.920
Help me!

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:15.420
This is...

00:22:21.470 --> 00:22:22.510
Kaito...

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.240 --> 00:24:03.440
Hey, what's going on?!

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:04.630
Is everyone okay?

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:06.260
Wait, I can't move!

00:24:06.260 --> 00:24:07.400
What is this place?

00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:09.540
Calm yourself, Gammon.

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:10.590
A Bodhisattva of Mercy!

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:13.820
Here, you are as immovable as a mountain.

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:15.890
Free yourself, Gammon!

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:18.260
A Boddisattva, and now this place...

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:19.560
Is this a dream?!

00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:26.670
The Awakening

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:21.660
Next time, "The Awakening"

00:24:21.660 --> 00:24:22.910
You got it!

00:24:22.910 --> 00:24:24.060
It's a dream!

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:25.590
So, it was a dream, huh?
